# MANDATORY: MCTB PAGE BUILD SPEC — 04: CONVERSATIONS

**Route:** `/mctb/conversations` or `/inbox?source=mctb` (canonical shared inbox + MCTB filter)  
**Source of truth:** `docs/TRANSOVO-MCTB-PAGE-BUILD-SPEC-04-CONVERSATIONS.md`  
**Prerequisites:** Governing MCTB docs + specs 01–03 + `transovo-mctb-page-build-specs.mdc`

## When this rule activates

**Before implementing, restyling, or declaring complete** MCTB Conversations workspace (`/mctb/conversations`, `/inbox` MCTB context, legacy `/voice/conversations`).

## Primary job

Read and respond to MCTB-originated SMS conversations from **one authoritative messaging workspace**.

## Hard architecture rule

**Do NOT build a duplicate MCTB inbox** if `/inbox` is canonical. Reuse shared Conversations engine + `source=mctb` filter + MCTB context links.

Legacy `/voice/conversations` → redirect to canonical MCTB Conversations or retire from MCTB IA.

## Workspace anatomy

Split-pane: conversation list | selected thread | optional context panel (missed call, contact).

- Deep link: `/mctb/conversations/:id` or equivalent
- No "New conversation" unless MCTB scope explicitly supports manual outbound
- Thread header: identity + *Started from missed call* + **View missed call**

## Message thread

- Actual historical content — compliance message ≠ business recovery message visually
- Opt-out as system event; suppressed ≠ sent bubble
- Delivery states from runtime — not provider jargon in thread

## Composer

Centralized eligibility before enable **and** recheck on send. Blocked states: opted out, sender unavailable, read-only, permission denied.

- No opt-out override / resubscribe without formal flow
- No duplicate send; preserve draft on recoverable failure
- Reply vs internal note explicit if notes supported

## Needs-reply

Centralized domain definition — must match Overview, Missed Calls, Detail.

## Prohibited

- Parallel MCTB conversation state model
- Campaign/marketing templates in MCTB context
- Fake message search; decorative attach; AI auto-send
- Misleading voice-conversations nav for SMS threads

## Definition of done

See full spec §102 checklist before marking Conversations complete.

